blocks:
  - type: metin
    baslik: What is a panic attack?
    metin: |-
      A panic attack is a sudden episode of intense fear or discomfort that typically lasts between a few minutes and half an hour. They often arise without an obvious trigger — they can occur in a shopping centre, in the car, or even during sleep.

      The brain receives a false danger signal and activates the ["fight or flight" response](/en/blog/brain-body-connection.html). The physical symptoms that follow are very real, but they are not medically dangerous.
  - type: bilgi-kutusu
    ton: yesil
    baslik: How common are panic attacks?
    metin: Approximately 11% of the world's population will experience at least one panic attack during their lifetime. [Panic disorder](/en/blog/what-is-anxiety-disorder.html) affects around 2–3% of adults and is twice as common in women. (APA, 2022)
  - type: kart-grid
    baslik: What are the symptoms of a panic attack?
    giris: 'According to DSM-5 diagnostic criteria, at least four of the following symptoms must arise abruptly and peak within minutes:'
    kolon: 2
    kartlar:
      - baslik: Physical
        maddeler:
          - Rapid or pounding heartbeat (palpitations)
          - Shortness of breath or feeling of choking
          - Chest pain or pressure
          - Trembling or shaking
          - Sweating, hot flushes
          - Nausea or stomach discomfort
          - Dizziness or light-headedness
          - Numbness or tingling
      - baslik: Psychological
        maddeler:
          - Fear of losing control or "going crazy"
          - Fear of dying
          - Sense of unreality (derealisation)
          - Feeling detached from oneself (depersonalisation)
